.TH OBJCOPY01 1 "October 2026" "mc6801-tools" "mc6801-tools Manual"
.SH NAME
objcopy01 \- convert MC6801 executables to loadable formats
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B objcopy01
.RB [ \-O
.IR format ]
.RB [ \-T
.IR textaddr ]
.RB [ \-D
.IR dataaddr ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-p ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR datasize ]
.RB [ \-v
.IR version ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.I infile outfile
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B objcopy01
reads an a.out executable produced by
.BR ld01 (1)
and writes its text and data segments to
.I outfile
in one of several formats for loaders, EPROM programmers and cassette
interfaces.
The input must have an a.out header, so do not link it with
.BR "ld01 \-d" .
.PP
The program\(aqs entry point is taken from the a.out header.
The load address should always be given with
.BR \-T ;
see BUGS.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-O " format"
Output format (default
.BR binary ).
See FORMATS.
.TP
.BI \-T " textaddr"
Load address of the text segment.
The value is read as a C number: decimal unless it has a
.B 0x
(hexadecimal) or
.B 0
(octal) prefix.
Note that this differs from
.BR "ld01 \-T" ,
which is always hexadecimal.
.TP
.BI \-D " dataaddr"
Load address of the data segment, for formats that can place it
separately.
If it is not given, the data segment follows the text segment.
.TP
.BI \-n " name"
Name to store in the output.
This is the S0 header record name for
.BR srec ,
the cassette file name for
.B cas
and
.B wav
(up to 8 characters, padded with spaces), and the module name for
.BR os9 .
The default is the output file name in upper case, including any
directory and suffix, so it is usually best to give
.B \-n
explicitly.
.TP
.B \-p
With
.BR binary ,
pad the gap between the text and data segments so that the data
appears at its correct offset.
.TP
.BI \-d " datasize"
.B os9
only: data area size to reserve.
.TP
.BI \-v " version"
.B os9
only: module version (0 to 127).
.TP
.B \-r
.B os9
only: mark the module re\-entrant.
.SH FORMATS
The format name may be abbreviated to its first three letters
.RB ( decb
and
.B ddos
need four).
.TP
.B binary
Raw memory image: the text segment followed by the data segment.
.TP
.B srec
Motorola S\-records: an S0 header containing the name, S1 data records
of 16 bytes, an S5 record count and an S9 record with the entry point.
.TP
.B ihex
Intel hex: 16\-byte data records and an end record holding the entry
point.
.TP
.B wav
Cassette audio as an 8\-bit mono WAV file at 43200 Hz, in the
Color BASIC tape format.
This format is also used by the Tandy MC\-10, which loads it with
.BR CLOADM .
Text and data must be contiguous.
.TP
.B cas
The same cassette data as
.BR wav ,
as a byte stream
.RB ( .cas
file) for emulators.
.TP
.B decb
Disk Extended Color BASIC
.B LOADM
binary (TRS\-80 Color Computer).
.TP
.B ddos
Dragon DOS binary.
Text and data must be contiguous.
.TP
.B os9
OS\-9 program module.
This is a 6809 format, inherited from the 6809 version of these tools.
.SH EXAMPLES
Make an MC\-10 cassette image loading at $434C:
.PP
.RS
.B objcopy01 \-O wav \-T 0x434c \-n MAIN main.aout main.wav
.RE
.PP
Make an S\-record file for an EPROM programmer:
.PP
.RS
.B objcopy01 \-O srec \-T 0xe000 \-n ROM rom.aout rom.s19
.RE
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
\(lq\fIformat\fP load address is zero\(rq means the load address was
not known; give
.BR \-T .
The matching \(lqdata load address is zero\(rq warning is harmless if the
program has no data segment.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ld01 (1),
.BR objdump01 (1),
.BR as01 (1)
.PP
The mc6801\-tools User\(aqs Manual
.RI ( mc6801\-tools\-manual.pdf ).
.SH BUGS
.B objcopy01
looks for the load addresses in the symbols
.BR __btext ,
.B __etext
and
.BR __bdata ,
but
.BR ld01 (1)
does not write these to the a.out symbol table.
So without
.BR \-T ,
the load address is taken to be 0 and the output is wrong for every
format except
.BR binary .
.SH AUTHOR
John W. Linville.
